@startuml 04-sequence-signup
title Sequence - Self-service sign-up, operator approval, key claim
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Applicant
actor Operator
participant "Web app" as Web
participant "API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Applicant -> Web : fill /signup form\n(company, contact, email, plan)
Web -> API : POST /signup-requests
API -> DB : INSERT signup_requests\n(status pending, claim code hash)
API --> Web : 201 { requestId, claimCode (shown once) }
Web --> Applicant : show request id + claim code

Applicant -> Web : /signup/status (id + code)
Web -> API : POST /signup-requests/status
API -> DB : find by id, compare code hash\n(constant time)
API --> Web : status: pending

Operator -> Web : Access requests page
Web -> API : GET /admin/signup-requests (operator JWT)
API --> Web : list + counts per status

alt approve
  Operator -> Web : Approve (plan, message)
  Web -> API : POST /admin/signup-requests/{id}/approve
  API -> DB : BEGIN; lock request\nINSERT account (placeholder key hash)\nmark approved; COMMIT
  API --> Web : approved
  Applicant -> Web : check status, "Get my API key"
  Web -> API : POST /signup-requests/claim (id + code)
  API -> DB : BEGIN; lock request\nreplace key hash, mark claimed; COMMIT
  API --> Web : { account, apiKey (once) }
  Web -> API : POST /auth/token (the new key)
  API --> Web : account JWT -> account portal
else deny
  Operator -> Web : Deny (reason required)
  Web -> API : POST /admin/signup-requests/{id}/reject
  API -> DB : mark rejected (note)
  Applicant -> Web : check status
  API --> Web : rejected + operator's reason
end

note over API, DB
  Wrong claim code and unknown id answer the same 404.
  One open request per email; one account per request.
end note
@enduml
